{
  "kind": "real-window probes (scratchpad S14Probe and the SwapProbe of 7a827e9), not a perf-suite capture: the suite never runs a live resize",
  "date": "2026-10-10 12:40-13:20 +01:00",
  "machine": "SPELDATOR, i7-14700K, RTX 4080 driver 610.62, Windows 11 26200; S14Probe on the 4K display at 150 %, SwapProbe at (100,100) on the 1440p display at 100 % with a 300 px bar",
  "configuration": "Release, HULTUI_A11Y=0, SDL_WINDOW_ACTIVATE_WHEN_SHOWN=0, P-cores; resize runs idle-gated; before and after alternated (before, after, before, after), JIT; AOT drag pair alternated once (results.AOT)",
  "probes": {
    "resize drag / toggle": "40 SetWindowPos steps (NOACTIVATE) on a Borderless Junction-like window: drag grows 12x8 px a step, toggle alternates two sizes; framesInside = frames drawn before SetWindowPos returned (counted by a 1x1 canvas), sameSize = frames at a size the step had already drawn, framesAfter = frames in the 3 unforced loop passes after each step; process and UI-thread CPU over the 40 steps",
    "invalidate": "InvalidateRect + UpdateWindow 20 times: a WM_PAINT each (EXPOSED, data1 0)",
    "exposed held": "SDL's live-resize timer simulated: EXPOSED with data1 1 pushed every 10 ms for 3 s while the loop is held (as in Win32's modal size/move loop)",
    "heldvideo": "the same for 2 s with mpv playing a 30 fps clip (libmpv-2.dll from native/mpv), frames drawn, frames mpv dropped, seconds played",
    "stretch sampling": "7a827e9's harness: 60 resizes of a TOPMOST, never-activated window while a second thread samples the screen for a 300 px white bar; frames = frames drawn in the 60 resizes"
  },
  "label": "gl-vk-resize-duplicate-frames, after: the watch draws a resize for a new size or a WM_PAINT, validates the client area after a frame, and otherwise draws only a dirty window or one with posted work waiting",
  "commit": "61edb19 + this change",
